WEBVTT

00:00:07.610 --> 00:00:08.650
It's finished!

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:22.210
And what have you been doing locked inside the prep room?

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.290
Another costume?

00:00:26.290 --> 00:00:27.290
Yes!

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:29.800
But this one's for you, Principal!

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:36.300
You always look so hot and sweaty in that suit.

00:00:36.670 --> 00:00:37.970
For me?

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.900
Aw, you shouldn't have.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:53.900
It's perfect! It really fits you well!

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:56.030
Really?

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.950
Shuwashuwa (Hi!) Shuwashuwa (Hi!)

00:00:58.450 --> 00:01:00.950
shuwashuwa (Hi!) shuwashuwa (Hi!)

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:03.450
Rainbow-colored (Wow!) morning shower

00:01:00.950 --> 00:01:03.450
nanairo (Wao!) mooningu shawaa

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.000
Good morning (Hi!) Good morning (Hi!)

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:06.000
ohayou (Hi!) ohayou (Hi!)

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.590
Raise your voice

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.590
ookina koe dashite

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:18.470
I liked my sketch until I woke up the next morning

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:18.470
shitagaki manzoku hitoban tatte kara

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:23.480
It sucks! It's terrible! I can't believe it's so bad!

00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:23.480
hetappi dameppi arienai yo

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:28.440
Ball it up and toss it out? Change the composition?

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:28.440
marumete suteyou ka kouzu wo kaeyou ka

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:33.030
Confused freckles. Yaino, yaino down

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:33.030
mayotta sobakasu yaino yaino daun

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:39.700
A peppy Special Gold (I'm full of energy)

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:39.700
genki na tokusei goorudo (genki desu)

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:44.750
Add more and (Your body will) leap up during a test

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:44.750
kasanetara (zenshin ga) tobiokiru tesuto chuu

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:49.670
(Cut and paste, but don't mess up the layout)

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:49.670
(kitte hatte reiauto kowasanaide)

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:55.970
It's like a blurry photo when you frown,

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:55.970
itsumo pinto boketa shashin mitai na

00:01:55.970 --> 00:02:00.350
So quit looking so depressed (Smile! Smile!)

00:01:55.970 --> 00:02:00.350
hekonda kao wa yosou (niko! niko!)

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:05.850
This warm canvas has always been right here

00:02:00.350 --> 00:02:05.850
itsumo koko deshita nukumori kyanbasu

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:10.230
Just hold on tight

00:02:05.850 --> 00:02:10.230
gyuutto dakishimete mite

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:13.400
Three musical notes ring out

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:13.400
oto mittsu dekita

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.990
Kushakusha (Hi!) Kushakusha (Hi!)

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.990
kushakusha (Hi!) kushakusha (Hi!)

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.570
In the dead of the night, (Wow!) a shooting star

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.570
mayonaka (Wao!) shuutingu sutaa

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:20.990
Good night (Good!) Good night (Good!)

00:02:18.570 --> 00:02:20.990
oyasumi (Goo!) oyasumi (Goo!)

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:24.410
I woke up when I heard you sleep talking...

00:02:20.990 --> 00:02:24.410
negoto de me ga sameta...

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.410
Whew.

00:02:24.410 --> 00:02:25.410
fuu.

00:02:34.490 --> 00:02:37.010
One, two, three, four!

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.510
Five, six, seven, eight!

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:42.010
Two, two, three, four!

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:44.600
Five, six, seven...

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:45.930
Huh?

00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:48.910
Good morning, Hiro!

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:50.440
Morning!

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.690
Yuno isn't here.

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:55.190
Oh, Yunocchi? She's—

00:02:55.190 --> 00:03:00.570
Yuno! Why did you abandon us!?

00:03:00.570 --> 00:03:02.320
It's not like that!

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:12.330
I'm home!

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:14.770
Welcome home, Yuno!

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:15.710
Welcome back!

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:18.710
Nyanta!

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.970
I missed you so much! How have you been?

00:03:22.970 --> 00:03:24.470
Nyanta...

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:30.070
I've been in such a tizzy since you told us you were coming home.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:36.230
I didn't have any homework over break, so I thought I could get away with coming back.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:40.320
Come on, it was pretty tough for your old man too.

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:46.530
I had to cancel all my work for the day, and I only got three hours of sleep last night.

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:49.790
I could've started getting ready if you'd told me sooner!

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:54.670
I'm sorry. I just really wanted to see your faces all of a sudden.

00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:59.670
You really need to think harder about our lives too!

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:02.930
Dad, your face doesn't match your words.

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:09.180
Seems like Yuno made it there fine.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.430
Yeah, she's gotta be there already.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:14.310
She left pretty early.

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:21.070
This is the first time Yuno's been gone. It feels a little lonely.

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:25.910
You're right. Yuno being gone makes you realize how great it is having her around.

00:04:26.450 --> 00:04:27.780
You too, Miyako?

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:34.880
Yeah. When I get hungry, I can't just follow my nose next door anymore.

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.210
That's what you miss!?

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:41.960
Okay, I made your favorite for dinner!

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:44.830
Wow, deviled pork!

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:46.270
That looks delicious.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:48.960
And some mackerel roasted in foil!

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.970
Wow, thanks! I love them both!

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:52.980
I'm so happy!

00:04:53.230 --> 00:04:54.850
All right, let's—

00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:59.480
And also some beef stew!

00:05:00.110 --> 00:05:03.770
And here's a Salisbury steak in my special sauce!

00:05:03.770 --> 00:05:06.860
Mom, this might be a bit much.

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:13.950
She fell asleep. The trip must have worn her out.

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:16.330
It does take a while to get here.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:19.630
If she had told us earlier, I would have driven out there to pick her up.

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:21.750
What?

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.840
With Yuno coming home all of a sudden,

00:05:23.840 --> 00:05:28.090
I figured she might be bringing someone along.

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:33.220
You mean Miya? Or Sae, or maybe Hiro?

00:05:33.220 --> 00:05:35.100
He doesn't even want to think about it, does he?

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:45.650
Good morning!
You look like you slept well.

00:05:45.650 --> 00:05:48.160
Wow, I slept clear until lunchtime.

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:52.260
Your dad fell back asleep after breakfast too.

00:05:52.240 --> 00:05:55.620
Oh, yeah. He did say he hadn't slept much.

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:56.750
My alarm!

00:05:58.500 --> 00:06:01.420
I wonder if he's having a nightmare.

00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:08.660
I'm going shopping. Do you want pork and potato stew for dinner?

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:11.210
Sure. I'll come along too.

00:06:11.210 --> 00:06:12.720
Oh, really?

00:06:17.180 --> 00:06:21.400
Oh my, if it isn't Yuno! It's been so long!

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:25.480
Oh, old Mrs. Miura!
I haven't seen you in a while!

00:06:25.510 --> 00:06:27.780
You've grown up so much!

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.780
You're a beautiful young lady now!

00:06:30.780 --> 00:06:33.440
Aw, you shouldn't.

00:06:33.440 --> 00:06:34.790
"Old"?

00:06:35.660 --> 00:06:37.790
She was really impressed with you.

00:06:37.790 --> 00:06:41.640
I don't feel like I've changed that much, though.

00:06:41.640 --> 00:06:43.920
You never realize that kind of thing yourself.

00:06:46.510 --> 00:06:48.140
Yuno!

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:48.760
Yuno?

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:53.440
Mayu! Manamin! Miyuki!

00:06:53.440 --> 00:06:55.640
It's been so long! You came back?

00:06:55.640 --> 00:06:58.140
Yeah, but only for a day.

00:06:58.390 --> 00:06:59.640
Wait...

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:03.180
Yuno, did you get shorter?

00:07:03.180 --> 00:07:04.760
Were you always this short?

00:07:04.770 --> 00:07:07.280
You're so tiny!

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:12.620
You have a supermarket near Hidamari Apartments, right?

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:16.370
It's not that close, but it's still in walking distance.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:20.200
Do you go together with everyone from Hidamari Apartments?

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:22.000
Yeah, we go all the time.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:25.630
Miya's great at hunting down free samples.

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:29.310
Sae's best at packing "all you can fit" bags.

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:33.010
And Hiro always picks out specials!

00:07:33.030 --> 00:07:35.510
Well, I guess you guys are scraping by.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:44.050
I wonder how long it's been since I cooked with you.

00:07:44.050 --> 00:07:47.530
What, didn't I help out sometimes?

00:07:47.530 --> 00:07:49.530
Did you?

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:55.200
Why don't you handle the seasoning and we'll
see how much you've learned living alone?

00:07:56.040 --> 00:07:57.790
I don't know if I can do it.

00:07:58.290 --> 00:08:00.540
I hope Dad will like it.

00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:02.670
I'm sure he will.

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:06.380
Yuno's... Yuno's cooking!

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:13.970
It came out great. Dad even had seconds.

00:08:14.420 --> 00:08:17.810
So, you're just taking it easy with your mom and dad?

00:08:17.810 --> 00:08:20.700
Yeah, it's nice and relaxing.

00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:23.150
What time are you getting back tomorrow?

00:08:23.150 --> 00:08:27.850
I'm leaving in the morning, so probably around dinner.

00:08:27.850 --> 00:08:30.190
Okay, take care.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:31.690
Yeah, thanks!

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:33.800
Miya—

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:36.450
Yunocchi?

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:41.040
Sorry about that. I'm fine. So, what's up with you?

00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:43.660
We all just slacked off.

00:08:43.660 --> 00:08:47.880
Oh, we had sandwiches for lunch, and Hiro—

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:50.960
Don't you dare, Miya!

00:08:50.960 --> 00:08:53.590
Aw, I was just getting to the good part.

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:55.840
There's nothing good about it!

00:08:55.840 --> 00:08:58.430
Hiro just wanted to try a bit of every kind.

00:08:58.430 --> 00:09:00.600
Even you, Sae!?

00:09:00.600 --> 00:09:02.980
Go easy on her. They were really good, after all.

00:09:04.050 --> 00:09:05.910
They were just so tasty!

00:09:05.910 --> 00:09:08.350
Yeah, they were really tasty!

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.320
And thus...

00:09:10.320 --> 00:09:12.070
Yunocchi, you listening?

00:09:12.070 --> 00:09:12.990
Yeah.

00:09:14.490 --> 00:09:16.210
Sleeping together?

00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:17.650
We should just about fit.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:18.780
Won't it be cramped?

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:22.370
It's been so long! We can sleep in the shape of the kanji for "river!"

00:09:22.370 --> 00:09:23.580
Yeah!

00:09:24.790 --> 00:09:26.290
Oh, Nyanta!

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:31.400
If Nyanta's sleeping with us, we can't be "river."

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:38.800
If I'm in the middle and Dad sideways on the bottom, we could be "mountain."

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:39.800
Mountain!?

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.390
I'm on the bottom!?

00:09:46.190 --> 00:09:50.270
You can always come home anytime.
It doesn't matter how sudden it is.

00:09:50.270 --> 00:09:51.080
Yeah.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:55.110
What is it?

00:09:55.130 --> 00:09:57.400
Something reminded me of Miss Yoshinoya.

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:03.650
She always tells people who choose solids that they can touch her boobs.

00:10:03.650 --> 00:10:05.410
What?

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:11.290
Thanks for seeing me off. I'm fine now, though.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:12.840
Take care!

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:13.920
Be sure to call.

00:10:14.320 --> 00:10:15.150
Sure!

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:18.250
See you!

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:23.930
See you, Yuno!

00:10:25.930 --> 00:10:27.940
I'm back!

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:32.230
That's amazing, Miyako!

00:10:32.250 --> 00:10:33.720
Like this?

00:10:33.730 --> 00:10:35.900
Hey Sae, that's cheating!

00:10:36.690 --> 00:10:38.700
I guess everyone's in there.

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.950
I'm back!

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:43.570
Welcome back!

00:10:43.570 --> 00:10:44.760
Welcome!

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:46.010
What are you doing?

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:49.080
We were talking about whether we could do handstands, and...

00:10:50.330 --> 00:10:51.960
Hi!

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:56.390
It felt great, like nothing had changed.

00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:59.100
It's always relaxing to be able to go home.

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:02.390
You probably wanted to stay longer, didn't you?

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:06.890
Yeah. I guess I'll be able to go back over summer vacation.

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:08.390
That's coming right up.

00:11:08.390 --> 00:11:09.090
Yeah.

00:11:09.090 --> 00:11:11.480
So, it's almost summer vacation.

00:11:11.900 --> 00:11:14.390
Though you have to study then.

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:16.610
Nothing wrong with a short trip.

00:11:16.610 --> 00:11:19.820
I hope we can all do something together.

00:11:19.820 --> 00:11:21.110
Yeah!

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:22.570
Of course. It's summer vacation!

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:24.830
I'd like to do something too.

00:11:48.660 --> 00:11:49.560
Miya!

00:11:51.090 --> 00:11:52.710
Morning, Yunocchi!

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:55.190
Good morning! What are you doing?

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:56.820
Getting the barbecue ready!

00:12:03.450 --> 00:12:06.740
What are you up to this early?

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:09.290
I was so hungry it woke me up!

00:12:09.290 --> 00:12:13.790
I want some meat, and the only cure for meatal hypophagia is barbecue!

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:15.170
Really?

00:12:15.170 --> 00:12:19.670
But if I barbecue in my room, I'm gonna have to pay for another haircut.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:26.180
Last year, Miya burned her bangs and had to go to Olive.

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:34.790
So once I figured there might be something
in the shed, I just couldn't stop myself.

00:12:34.790 --> 00:12:36.410
Good work finding it.

00:12:36.410 --> 00:12:38.400
It should work fine if we clean it up.

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:45.240
I knew the girls who lived here before us would leave us one.

00:12:46.240 --> 00:12:48.240
We don't have any charcoal, though, do we?

00:12:48.610 --> 00:12:51.530
If we need charcoal, I've got some.

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:55.120
Looks like you're really prepared!

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:58.460
She's joking, Nazuna.

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:03.170
I guess we'd need to go buy charcoal.

00:13:03.170 --> 00:13:07.300
Come on, let's all have a barbecue!

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:08.940
Yeah, it sounds fun.

00:13:08.940 --> 00:13:10.090
Agreed!

00:13:10.090 --> 00:13:11.060
Me too!

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:12.650
It can't hurt from time to time.

00:13:12.650 --> 00:13:15.810
Yeah, we've all been studying so much that we need a break.

00:13:15.810 --> 00:13:18.810
All right! Barbecue!

00:13:18.810 --> 00:13:21.010
Okay, let's go shopping!

00:13:21.010 --> 00:13:22.320
Yeah!

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:27.530
First, we need—

00:13:27.530 --> 00:13:28.530
Meat!

00:13:32.240 --> 00:13:34.630
Some seafood would be nice too.

00:13:34.630 --> 00:13:36.390
Yeah, like shrimp and scallops!

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:37.310
And squid!

00:13:37.310 --> 00:13:39.130
Dried fish!

00:13:40.120 --> 00:13:41.620
Barbecued?

00:13:41.620 --> 00:13:45.280
Hiro and Sae aren't going to like it if you pick weird stuff.

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:48.510
Dried fish isn't weird! It's good!

00:13:50.410 --> 00:13:52.350
Huh? Where's Nazuna?

00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:54.350
She was here just a second ago.

00:13:56.430 --> 00:13:57.350
Um...

00:13:58.100 --> 00:14:00.360
Can we toast these?

00:14:04.810 --> 00:14:05.610
It's hot.

00:14:05.610 --> 00:14:08.950
Great weather for a barbecue.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:10.280
Yeah.

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:15.580
Yuno and the others are done shopping too.

00:14:18.830 --> 00:14:21.350
Oh, hi, Natsume.

00:14:21.350 --> 00:14:23.140
Yo! Where are you off to?

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:26.210
I was going over to a friend's.

00:14:27.220 --> 00:14:28.680
What are you up to?

00:14:28.680 --> 00:14:31.000
We're having a barbecue in the back yard.

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:35.180
That's not a very good use of your time with entrance exams coming up!

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:38.360
You're the one going over to a friend's!

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:40.920
I'm going to study!

00:14:40.920 --> 00:14:41.690
Sae...

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:44.980
How about coming over afterward, Natsume?

00:14:45.740 --> 00:14:46.940
Hiro...

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:49.360
There's nothing wrong with taking a breather.

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:53.030
It is our last summer vacation in high school, after all.

00:14:54.110 --> 00:14:55.240
Come on over later.

00:14:55.240 --> 00:14:56.750
What are—

00:15:01.290 --> 00:15:02.420
It's hot!

00:15:02.420 --> 00:15:04.210
It should be about ready.

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:07.210
All right, we're good to go!

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:08.800
Okay!

00:15:10.760 --> 00:15:12.550
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:14.430
Dried fish?

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:17.130
It smells great!

00:15:17.750 --> 00:15:19.880
I'm starving!

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:22.560
I skipped breakfast.

00:15:22.560 --> 00:15:23.720
You too?

00:15:23.720 --> 00:15:25.440
I can hardly wait.

00:15:26.190 --> 00:15:30.450
Who made this one? It's all meat.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:31.700
I did!

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:36.830
Cheers!

00:15:40.670 --> 00:15:42.340
I feel alive again!

00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:45.170
Yeah, it tingles!

00:15:46.920 --> 00:15:48.670
Let's eat!

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:52.320
It's still hot!

00:15:52.320 --> 00:15:53.760
It's done, right?

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:56.260
It's perfect!

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:01.140
So juicy!

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:05.560
Nazuna, let's toast the marshmallows.

00:16:05.560 --> 00:16:07.190
Toast marshmallows?

00:16:07.190 --> 00:16:09.190
It was Nazuna's idea.

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:16.070
I can't even imagine what they'll taste like.

00:16:16.870 --> 00:16:22.620
It's so fluffy and airy, but warm and melty at the same time!

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:23.870
You did just grill it.

00:16:26.450 --> 00:16:27.990
I think they're done.

00:16:27.990 --> 00:16:28.920
Thanks.

00:16:29.170 --> 00:16:31.090
Here goes.

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:36.050
How are they?

00:16:36.090 --> 00:16:40.020
It's fluffy and airy and melty!

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:46.020
Yeah! The outside is crispy, but the marshmallow inside is melted!

00:16:46.020 --> 00:16:47.240
That makes more sense.

00:16:47.240 --> 00:16:48.570
This was a great idea.

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:53.920
Can I cook this too?

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:56.200
You bought dried fish?

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:59.230
You're the only one that even eats that stuff.

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:03.170
Main dish!

00:17:03.170 --> 00:17:05.500
Dried fish?

00:17:08.360 --> 00:17:10.340
Miya! Fan it away!

00:17:10.340 --> 00:17:11.800
Roger that!

00:17:18.040 --> 00:17:18.680
Oh my!

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:28.060
Natsume!

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:31.570
Are they not home?

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:33.350
They're here.

00:17:34.570 --> 00:17:35.570
Look out!

00:17:35.570 --> 00:17:36.570
Smoke!?

00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:37.320
Oh no!

00:17:38.820 --> 00:17:39.800
Sae!

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:43.700
It's cleared up.

00:17:43.700 --> 00:17:45.410
Sheesh.

00:17:45.430 --> 00:17:46.960
Looks great, doesn't it?

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:47.960
Sae!

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:50.590
Are you guys okay!?

00:17:50.590 --> 00:17:52.210
Miss Yoshinoya!

00:17:52.210 --> 00:17:53.090
Natsume!

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:58.750
Oh, you frightened me.

00:17:58.750 --> 00:18:02.850
There was so much smoke that I thought something had happened.

00:18:02.850 --> 00:18:06.980
Sorry, the dried fish was smokier than we expected.

00:18:07.350 --> 00:18:09.230
I'm just glad it wasn't a fire.

00:18:09.230 --> 00:18:10.650
You're overreacting.

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:12.900
It's not like I was worried or anything!

00:18:12.900 --> 00:18:16.610
Would you like some, Miss Yoshinoya?

00:18:16.610 --> 00:18:17.900
Thank you!

00:18:17.900 --> 00:18:19.410
You too, Natsume!

00:18:20.280 --> 00:18:21.410
I...

00:18:21.880 --> 00:18:23.940
That's why you came, right?

00:18:23.940 --> 00:18:25.290
It came out great!

00:18:28.290 --> 00:18:29.440
Sae...

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:35.300
Oh, right. We ran into her while we were shopping.

00:18:35.300 --> 00:18:37.840
This is Natsume from third year class B.

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:41.160
I'm Nori from first year class A.

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:43.470
I'm Nazuna from first year class D.

00:18:44.460 --> 00:18:45.720
I'm Natsume.

00:18:46.980 --> 00:18:47.810
Here.

00:18:48.180 --> 00:18:49.130
Thanks.

00:18:49.130 --> 00:18:52.940
Well then, don't mind if I do!

00:18:56.170 --> 00:18:57.190
It's so tasty!

00:18:57.190 --> 00:18:59.820
You were at school, Miss Yoshinoya?

00:18:59.820 --> 00:19:05.330
Even if you're on summer vacation, we teachers have to go to school every day.

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:07.160
I'm just on lunch break.

00:19:07.950 --> 00:19:17.240
I want to enjoy summer vacation and make
once-in-a-lifetime memories just like you,

00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:22.180
but the Principal gave me a ton of work to do!

00:19:23.300 --> 00:19:26.950
And I had my summer all planned out!

00:19:26.950 --> 00:19:28.560
What is she, an elementary schooler?

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:31.850
That was great.

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:36.860
It's getting pretty late.
I have to get back to school.

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:39.110
Thanks for the help!

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:44.950
Okay, guys! It's good to relax, but make sure to do your homework too!

00:19:44.950 --> 00:19:46.240
Okay!

00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:50.120
Be sure to have a wonderful summer vacation you'll remember forever!

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.370
Okay!

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:55.130
But don't go growing up too fast.

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:56.630
Okay.

00:19:57.250 --> 00:20:02.430
Okay, good. Be careful around the fire!

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:03.590
Okay!

00:20:06.720 --> 00:20:08.720
Nori!

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:16.420
Okay!

00:20:16.420 --> 00:20:18.110
You too, Hiro!

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:19.980
Say cheese!

00:20:21.600 --> 00:20:23.550
Can you send it to my phone?

00:20:23.550 --> 00:20:24.200
Sure.

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:29.290
Me too, me too!

00:20:29.290 --> 00:20:30.120
You want to take a picture?

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:31.370
Here.

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:36.380
How'd it come out?

00:20:38.590 --> 00:20:40.590
Give me your number and I'll send you a copy.

00:20:49.890 --> 00:20:51.680
I'm so full!

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:54.170
I couldn't eat another bite.

00:20:54.170 --> 00:20:55.650
I don't think I'll need dinner.

00:20:56.130 --> 00:20:58.270
Thanks for today.

00:20:58.270 --> 00:20:59.770
What's this all of a sudden?

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:01.400
I had fun.

00:21:01.400 --> 00:21:02.610
That's great.

00:21:04.610 --> 00:21:06.740
I'm glad we barbecued.

00:21:07.420 --> 00:21:10.120
But I still haven't made any precious memories!

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:14.020
Summer vacation's only just started, Miya.

00:21:20.600 --> 00:21:23.300
Today was fun.

00:21:23.310 --> 00:21:26.180
It's nice eating outside.

00:21:28.180 --> 00:21:32.680
I think I tanned a bit from being out in the sun all day.

00:21:40.060 --> 00:21:44.110
What do I do? I'm hungry so late.

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:51.850
Thanks, Hiro!

00:21:51.850 --> 00:21:53.780
I figured I had to.

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:57.830
I bet these rice balls would be even better if we barbecued them!

00:21:57.830 --> 00:22:00.130
Maybe next time.

00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:05.470
Let's eat!

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:16.940
I first met you on a fresh new spring day

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:16.940
atarashii haru no hi kimi to deatta

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:21.310
A flower blossomed in my heart, a flower in full bloom

00:22:16.560 --> 00:22:21.310
kokoro ni hana ga saku mankai no hana

00:22:21.310 --> 00:22:29.490
I can see cherry blossoms from my window

00:22:21.310 --> 00:22:29.490
sakura ga mieru yo mado kara

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:37.290
Another spring went by, but my feelings haven't changed

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:37.290
nidome no haru ga sugi kawaranai omoi

00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:42.000
I'll try to close the distance lingering between us

00:22:37.370 --> 00:22:42.000
chijimanakatta kyori arukidashite miyou

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:47.800
I waited for you along the path you take home,

00:22:42.170 --> 00:22:47.800
guuzen wo yosootte kimi wo

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:51.800
But I pretended it was just a coincidence

00:22:47.800 --> 00:22:51.800
kaeri michi machibuse shita

00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:57.600
The flower petals in my palm swayed in the breeze

00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:57.600
te no hira ni hanabira hirari

00:22:57.730 --> 00:23:04.770
Your smile and the scenery are seared into my eyes

00:22:57.730 --> 00:23:04.770
kimi no egao me ni yakitsuketa keshiki

00:23:04.770 --> 00:23:10.200
The cherry blossoms are flowering, and I want to see you

00:23:04.770 --> 00:23:10.200
sakura saku kimi ni aitai

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:15.080
If only I could always be with you

00:23:10.200 --> 00:23:15.080
kimi to zutto ireta nara

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:21.210
So many cherry blossoms are flowering

00:23:15.080 --> 00:23:21.210
sakura sakura saiteru suki dayo

00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:31.010
I can feel this shining season in my heart, and I love it

00:23:21.210 --> 00:23:31.010
koko ni aru kagayaita kisetsu wo
